body:
### Tested versions

- Reproducible in 4.6 Mono

### System information

Godot v4.6.stable.mono - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9571) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900KF (32 threads) - 31.81 GiB memory

### Issue description

When dragging a Node with a custom Script on an exported property to reference it, it results in an error. 

I know this error and solved it sometimes already in different cases but I can not explain why it is happening in the MRP.

I want to drag the "Health" class on to the Health Property in the Entity Class.

```
using Godot;
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

[Tool]
public partial class Entity : StaticBody2D, IHealth {
    public event Action<float> HealthChanged;
    public event Action<float> HealthIncreased;
    public event Action<float> HealthDecreased;

    public bool IsDead { get; set; }

    [Export]
    private Health _Health;

    /// <summary>
    /// <inheritdoc cref="Health.Decrease"/><br/>
    /// <br/>
    /// Wrapper Method for <see cref="Health.Decrease"/>
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="amount"></param>
    public void DecreaseHealth(float amount) {
        this._Health.Decrease(amount);
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// <inheritdoc cref="Health.Increase"/><br/>
    /// <br/>
    /// Wrapper Method for <see cref="Health.Increase"/>
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="amount"></param>
    public void IncreaseHealth(float amount) {
        this._Health.Increase(amount);
    }
}
```

```
public partial class Health : Node {
    /// <summary>
    /// Event triggered when the health reaches 0. This event is only triggered once when the health transitions from above 0 to 0 or below.
    /// </summary>
    public event Action Died;

    /// <summary>
    /// Event triggered when the health changes. The float parameter represents the new health amount
    /// </summary>
    public event Action<float> Changed;

    /// <summary>
    /// Event triggered when the health is increased. The float parameter represents the amount of increase.
    /// </summary>
    public event Action<float> Increased;

    /// <summary>
    /// Event triggered when the health is decreased. The float parameter represents the amount of decrease.
    /// </summary>
    public event Action<float> Decreased;

    /// <summary>
    /// Maximum possible amount of <see cref="Amount">Health</see>
    /// </summary>
    public float MaxAmount { get; private set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Current amount of Health
    /// </summary>
    public float Amount {
        get;
        private set {
            field = value;
            this.Changed?.Invoke(value);
        }
    }

    public bool IsDead => this.Amount <= 0;

    public override void _EnterTree() {
        this._RegisterCallbacks();
    }

    private void _RegisterCallbacks() {
        this.Changed += this._OnHealthChanged;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Decreases the <see cref="Amount">Health</see> by the specified amount. If the resulting amount is less than 0, it will be set to 0.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="amount"></param>
    public void Decrease(float amount) {
        var newAmount = this.Amount - amount;
        if (newAmount < 0) {
            newAmount = 0;
        }

        this.Amount = newAmount;
        this.Decreased?.Invoke(amount);
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Increases the <see cref="Amount">Health</see> by the specified amount. <br/>
    /// If the resulting amount is greater than <see cref="MaxAmount">MaxAmount</see>, it will be set to <see cref="MaxAmount">MaxAmount</see>.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="amount"></param>
    public void Increase(float amount) {
        var newAmount = this.Amount + amount;
        if (newAmount > this.MaxAmount) {
            newAmount = this.MaxAmount;
        }

        this.Amount = newAmount;
        this.Increased?.Invoke(amount);
    }

    private bool _TryKill(float amount) {
        if (amount > 0) {
            return false;
        }

        this.Kill();
        return true;
    }

    public void Kill() {
        this.Died?.Invoke();
    }

    private void _OnHealthChanged(float newAmount) {
        this._TryKill(newAmount);
    }
}
```

The error appears even the Node has the Health class attached and it inherits from the same Node type.

<img width="2316" height="106" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1c13532f-2211-4f55-a1b3-284a6cb696a0" />

### Steps to reproduce

In the MRP:

1. Select the Entity
2. Drag the Health Node on to the exported Health Property from the Entity
3. Error appears

